---
import BaseLayout from "../../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../site/styles/comparison-label-study.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Comparison label study — Mourne Made" description="A visual study of comparison labels for Mourne Made." hideFooter>
  <main class="comparison-label-study">
    <div class="shell comparison-label-study-intro">
      <a class="comparison-label-study-back" href="/prototypes/comparison-control-study/">← Comparison control study</a>
      <p class="home-kicker">Mourne Made · component study</p>
      <h1>How should the comparison explain itself?</h1>
      <p class="comparison-label-study-lede">Three treatments for the small labels that tell visitors which side they’re viewing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell comparison-label-study-grid">
      <article class="comparison-label-option"><p class="comparison-label-option-name"><span>A</span> Corner labels</p><div class="label-demo label-demo--corners"><b>BEFORE</b><b>AFTER</b></div><p>Directly tied to each image. The labels stay out of the control area.</p></article>
      <article class="comparison-label-option"><p class="comparison-label-option-name"><span>B</span> Legend row</p><div class="label-demo label-demo--legend"><b>Before</b><i>Drag to compare</i><b>After</b></div><p>A single line explains both sides and the action in one place.</p></article>
      <article class="comparison-label-option"><p class="comparison-label-option-name"><span>C</span> Minimal sides</p><div class="label-demo label-demo--minimal"><b>Before</b><b>After</b></div><p>Small, quiet labels that let the image comparison lead completely.</p></article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
